# PATCH - Apply a verified binary patch

```text
PATCH patchfile [/INPUT=file] [/OUTPUT=file]
```

## Apply a patch

A patch file supplies the input and output names or you can override
them. PATCH checks the expected bytes before creating a separate output
file, then reads back the patched copy.

```text
C0:PATCH FIX.PAT /INPUT=D0:OLD.COM /OUTPUT=D0:NEW.COM
```

## Read an instruction

```text
0120: CD 05 00 C9 -> 00 00
```

At hexadecimal file offset 0120 the four original bytes must match.
PATCH replaces the first two, leaving 00 C9 in place. A mismatch stops
the operation. Use [DUMP](DUMP.HLP) to inspect the input at the reported
offset.
